er</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>2006</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>3089</fpage><lpage>94</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16809734</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-co14_6p238"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Simons</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Sacks</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Granulocyte&#x02013;macrophage colony&#x02013;stimulating factor&#x02013;transduced allogeneic cancer cellular immunotherapy: the Gvax vaccine for prostate cancer</article-title><source>Urol Oncol</source><year>2006</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>419</fpage><lpage>24</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16962494</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17-co14_6p238"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Small</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Higano</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Analysis of prognostic variables in phase <sc>ii</sc> trials of Gvax vaccine for prostate cancer in metastatic hormone refractory prostate cancer [abstract 254]</article-title><conf-name>Abstracts of the 2006 Prostate Cancer Symposium</conf-name><conf-loc>San Francisco, CA</conf-loc><conf-date>February 24&#x02013;26, 2006</conf-date><publisher-loc>Alexandria, VA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>American Society of Clinical Oncology</publisher-name><year>2006</year><comment>[Web resource] Available under &#x0201c;Abstracts &#x00026; Virtual Meeting&#x0201d; at: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="www.asco.org">www.asco.org</ext-link></comment><access-date>cited: June 12, 2007</access-date></citation></ref><ref id="b18-co14_6p238"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sim